{"id": "EUVD-2026-80531", "enisaUuid": "570782fb-ed75-342d-8481-557b990d4b93", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKVM: nVMX: Ensure KVM_REQ_GET_NESTED_STATE_PAGES is cleared on VM-Exit\n\nAlways check and clear KVM_REQ_GET_NESTED_STATE_PAGES when emulating a\nnested VM-Exit to ensure the request is cleared, even when KVM was built\nwith CONFIG_KVM_HYPERV=n, as KVM subtly relies on the \"check\" to clear\nthe flag and thus avoid double-mapping the vmcs12 pages, e.g. if KVM\nmanages to bail from VM-Enter without processing the request, and then\nemulates VMLAUNCH or VMRESUME.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:32:22", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:55:05", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ae190f2439ca30067927077bf570d4c5edf07a0f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/674a3244f07f323f21a106a7bdcaebb6db6a5058", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bbec4adc2f340d85f4a77a9ddcddaa6b1f4639c5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/11722439fb206c88e6f31be54173efa9880b4ccb"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89931", "GHSA-9jg7-wvq2-32v3"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1ce2dcaf-f409-3def-b9fd-468319623f55", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.8"}, {"id": "2135a854-915a-3959-838a-03f1f7bf43ca", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b4f69df0f65e97fec439130a0d0a8b9c7cc02df2 <bbec4adc2f340d85f4a77a9ddcddaa6b1f4639c5"}, {"id": "2fc7b29b-1eea-3834-827f-b915696f4d09", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "89b6c272-99f9-3bee-9d6f-89b5d2ea05f3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "9c7da82a-2211-371a-a8ab-2f5508b9d4f4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b4f69df0f65e97fec439130a0d0a8b9c7cc02df2 <11722439fb206c88e6f31be54173efa9880b4ccb"}, {"id